===Etymology===
From {{lbor|en|la|cotylēdōn|notext=1}}, from {{der|en|grc|κοτυληδών|t=cup-shaped cavity}}, from {{m|grc|κοτύλη|t=cup}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˌkɒt.ɪˈliː.dən/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cotyledon.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˌkɑt.əˈliː.dən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|physiology}} Each of the patches of [[villi]] on the [[foetal]] [[chorion]] in the [[placenta]] of [[ruminant]]s and some other mammals.
#* '''1997''', {{w|Roy Porter}}, ''The Greatest Benefit to Mankind'', Folio Society 2016, p. 72:
#*: Forced to apply animal findings to humans, his human womb also had '''cotyledons''' like a dog's.
# {{lb|en|botany}} The [[leaf]] of the [[embryo]] of a [[seed]]-[[bearing]] [[plant]]; after [[germination]] it becomes the first leaves of the [[seedling]].

